  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decreasing the impact of threats on the great apes of the proposed Ebo National Park, Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to contribute to the development of the future Ebo National Park and reduce threats to great ape populations. Specific activities include: (1) reducing hunting by people living in the immediate vicinity of the forest through a variety of community education activities such as Clubs des Amis des Gorilles, supporting pro-conservation decisions made by local leaders, and limiting damage to habitat and biodiversity by collaborating with other NGOs to provide time-sensitive information on commercial activities; (2) providing a permanent presence at two field stations through regular habitat monitoring, patrols of the gorilla range, and the development of a reconnaissance unit; and (3) enabling communication, coordination and collaboration among key organizations, including MINFOF, traditional authorities and local leaders to decrease threats to ape populations.</narrative>
  </description>
